# Line endings are LF in the repository and in every checkout, on every OS.
#
# Lane 0.8 (found 2026-08-13): with no .gitattributes and core.autocrlf=true,
# a Windows checkout held CRLF while the index and CI's checkout held LF, so
# byte-level comparisons drifted locally (245 CRLF vs 245 LF read as a change)
# while passing in CI, and 26 files had been committed with CRLF or mixed
# endings by whichever editor touched them last. Declaring eol=lf here makes
# the working copy match the index, so a diff is only ever content.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect binaries it does not know; the explicit entries
# below cover the ones it must never touch.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalized, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pfx binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Windows batch files are the one text format that genuinely needs CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
